    -variables can be stored by "<-" to view the variable's value, type it again (keyboard shortcut: Alt + -)
        EX: x <- 3 * 4
            x
            #> [1] 12
    -combine multiple elements into a vector by adding c()
    -seq() makes sequences 
        EX: seq(from = 1, to = 10) OR seq(1, 10)
    -parenthesis and quotations must come in pair
Takeaway: Be careful about human error mistakes when naming and setting variables, use keyboard shortcuts, comment the "why" not the "how"

